# Blender owns authoring; CidbTool owns the binary bake (its PhysX 3.4 cooker
# port is verified byte-exact against every retail mesh). This add-on is the
# bridge: readable collision materials, preset assignment, primitive shapes,
# and a Bake button that runs CidbTool.
#
# Data model
#   * A face's collision behaviour is its material. Every LAS collision
#     material carries the full u32 contact code in material["las_contact_code"]
#     and is named after the matching retail preset ("LAS Stone · Dungeon").
#   * Imported faces also keep their original identity as face attributes
#     (las_surface_id, las_face_remap, las_extra_flag). When a face still has
#     its original code, the export writes that original slot + remap so an
#     untouched room bakes back byte-identically; changed or new faces are
#     written as full contact codes.
#   * Box/sphere primitive sections become objects with las_primitive set.

